+# Threshold Support Implementation Summary
+
+This document summarizes the implementation of threshold support for `frai eval` as specified in SPEC.md.
+
+## Changes Made
+
+### 1. Core Evaluation Module (`packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.js`)
+
+**Modified `generateReport()` function:**
+- Added optional `thresholds` parameter (object mapping metric IDs to minimum values)
+- When thresholds are provided:
+  - Evaluates each threshold against computed metrics
+  - Creates a thresholdResults array with metric ID, min, score, and pass/fail status
+  - Adds `passed` (boolean) and `thresholds` (array) fields to report
+  - Returns object with `report` and `passed` properties
+- When thresholds are NOT provided:
+  - Returns report directly (backward compatible)
+  - Does NOT include `passed` or `thresholds` fields
+
+### 2. Report Formatters (`packages/frai-core/src/eval/reporters.js`)
+
+**Modified `toMarkdown()` function:**
+- Added "Thresholds" section when report contains thresholds array
+- Shows ✓ PASS or ✗ FAIL status for each threshold
+- Displays metric name, minimum value, and actual score
+- Shows "N/A" for null scores
+
+**JSON formatting (via `toJson()`):**
+- Automatically includes `passed` and `thresholds` fields when present (no changes needed)
+
+### 3. CLI (`packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`)
+
+**Updated `EvalOptions` interface:**
+- Added `threshold?: string[]` field
+
+**Added threshold parsing functions:**
+- `parseThreshold()`: Parses `<metric>=<value>` format
+  - Validates exactly one `=` separator
+  - Validates value is a valid number between 0 and 1
+  - Throws descriptive errors on validation failure
+
+- `buildThresholdsMap()`: Converts threshold strings to metric->min object
+  - Handles multiple thresholds for same metric by taking the maximum (strictest)
+  - Returns undefined when no thresholds provided
+
+- `validateThresholds()`: Validates thresholds against evaluated metrics
+  - Checks that each metric ID exists in evaluations
+  - Lists all valid metric IDs in error message
+
+**Updated `runEvalCommand()` function:**
+- Parses and validates thresholds before evaluation
+- Exits with code 2 if threshold format is invalid
+- Exits with code 2 if metric is unknown (with valid metrics list)
+- Passes thresholds to generateReport
+- Handles both return types from generateReport (backward compatible)
+- Writes report regardless of pass/fail status
+- Exits with code 1 if thresholds are not met
+- Exits with code 0 if all thresholds pass or no thresholds specified
+
+**Updated eval command definition:**
+- Added `--threshold <metric>=<value>` option (repeatable)
+- Help text: "Quality gate: metric minimum score (0-1, repeatable; e.g., --threshold exact_match=0.9 --threshold bleu=0.8)"
+
+### 4. Tests (`packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.test.js`)
+
+**Added comprehensive tests:**
+- `passes thresholds when score meets minimum`: Exit 0 scenario
+- `fails thresholds when score does not meet minimum`: Exit 1 scenario
+- `handles missing scores with null`: Null score handling
+- `maintains backward compatibility without thresholds`: No-threshold scenario
+- `handles multiple thresholds for different metrics`: Multiple metric test
+- `reports overall failed status when any threshold fails`: Partial failure test
+- `writes markdown report with thresholds section`: Markdown format test
+- `writes json report with thresholds`: JSON format test
+
+## Behavior
+
+### Exit Codes
+- **0**: All thresholds passed, or no thresholds specified
+- **1**: At least one threshold failed (report written)
+- **2**: Usage error (malformed threshold or unknown metric, no report written)
+
+### Threshold Validation
+- Format: `<metric>=<number>` (case-sensitive metric ID)
+- Value range: 0 to 1 (inclusive)
+- Multiple thresholds for same metric: all must pass (uses maximum/strictest threshold)
+
+### Report Format
+When thresholds are specified:
+- JSON includes `passed` (boolean) and `thresholds` (array) at top level
+- Markdown includes "Thresholds" section before "Metrics" section
+- Each threshold entry shows: metric ID, minimum value, actual score, pass/fail status
+
+When no thresholds specified:
+- JSON/Markdown format unchanged (backward compatible)
+- No `passed` or `thresholds` fields
+
+### Error Handling
+- Malformed format: descriptive error message, exit 2
+- Invalid value (not a number): descriptive error message, exit 2
+- Value outside range: descriptive error message, exit 2
+- Unknown metric: lists all valid metrics in error message, exit 2
+
+## SDK Usage
+
+```javascript
+const result = generateReport({
+  evaluations,
+  outputsPath: '/path/to/outputs.json',
+  referencesPath: '/path/to/references.json',
+  thresholds: {
+    exact_match: 0.9,
+    toxicity: 0.95
+  }
+});
+
+if (result.passed) {
+  console.log('All thresholds passed');
+} else {
+  console.log('Threshold evaluation:', result.report.thresholds);
+}
+```
+
+## CLI Usage
+
+```bash
+# Exit 0: thresholds pass
+frai eval --outputs outputs.json --references refs.json --threshold exact_match=0.9 --threshold toxicity=0.95
+
+# Exit 1: thresholds fail
+frai eval --outputs outputs.json --references refs.json --threshold exact_match=0.99
+
+# Exit 2: malformed threshold
+frai eval --outputs outputs.json --threshold "exact_match"
+
+# Exit 2: unknown metric
+frai eval --outputs outputs.json --threshold unknown_metric=0.8
+```
+
+## Backward Compatibility
+
+The implementation maintains full backward compatibility:
+- Without `--threshold` option, behavior is identical to original
+- `generateReport()` without thresholds parameter returns just the report
+- Report format unchanged when no thresholds provided
+- Exit codes match original behavior (0 on success, errors handled normally)
+
+## Testing
+
+To verify implementation, run:
+```bash
+npm test  # Runs all tests including new threshold tests
+```
+
+Known test status:
+- Two existing tests fail on main (pre-existing, tracked separately)
+- All new threshold tests should pass
+- Gate tests should pass
